{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsKnots.nsi_q_deformed_kernel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.nsi_q_deformed_kernel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Order.Field","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.nsi_q_deformed_kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.nsi_q_deformed_kernel","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L179-L201","doc":"**`q`-deformed commutator replaces `1/r²` with a hard kernel at\n`r = ℏ_q`** ([`lem:nsi-q-deformed-kernel`]) — the resolving\ndeclaration for `lean.ref`\n`qou:QOU.BraidsKnots.nsi_q_deformed_kernel`.\n\nConjoins the two parts of the manuscript lemma: (1) the\nidentification of the inherited trace-side kernel with\n`[2]_q / (r² − ℏ_q²)` at `r = ‖ϱ(s) − ϱ(t)‖` (**sorry-free but\n§3b-conditional** — `nsi_q_kernel_identification` derives it from the\ncontext's `K_cat_eq` / `qDeformedCommutator_eq` hypothesis fields,\nwhich is where the un-formalised commutator content sits), and (2) the\nhard singularity at `r = ℏ_q` (**derived sorry-free** in\n`nsi_q_kernel_hard_singularity` from the concrete kernel).\nNeither conjunct projects a conclusion field. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:nsi-q-deformed-kernel","label":"lem:nsi-q-deformed-kernel","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/nsi-q-deformed-kernel.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.nsi_q_kernel_identification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.nsi_q_kernel_identification","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L164-L177","doc":"**Identification of the inherited kernel** — the trace-side\nkernel of the filament's categorical mass equals the concrete\n`q`-deformed kernel `[2]_q / (‖ϱ(s) − ϱ(t)‖² − ℏ_q²)` for\n`q ≠ 1`.  Sorry-free, but §3b-**conditional** on\n`NsiQDeformedKernelContext`: the un-formalised content (the\n`q`-deformed commutator and `q`-Hodge star) is carried as the explicit\nhypothesis fields `K_cat_eq` and `qDeformedCommutator_eq`, from which\nthe identification is derived.  The premise is assumed, not\nestablished — see AGENTS.md §\"Conditional-proved ≠ premise-established\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.qDeformedCommutator_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.qDeformedCommutator_eq","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L162-L162","doc":"The q-deformed commutator matches the concrete q-deformed kernel for q ≠ 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.K_cat_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.K_cat_eq","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L160-L160","doc":"The categorical kernel is derived from the q-deformed commutator evaluated on the filament. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.qDeformedCommutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.qDeformedCommutator","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L158-L158","doc":"The q-deformed commutator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.K_cat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.K_cat","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L156-L156","doc":"Trace-side kernel `K_cat s t` inherited by the categorical mass\nof the filament (the `q`-deformed commutator's replacement of\nthe classical `1/r²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.ϱ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.ϱ","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L152-L152","doc":"Vortex filament curve `ϱ : ℝ → E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.q","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L150-L150","doc":"Substrate deformation parameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L148-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.NsiQDeformedKernelContext","kind":"class","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L145-L162","doc":"Data of the NSI `q`-deformed-kernel claim\n([`lem:nsi-q-deformed-kernel`]).  All fields are *inputs*; none\nis the conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.nsi_q_kernel_hard_singularity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.nsi_q_kernel_hard_singularity","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L96-L143","doc":"**Hard singularity at `r = ℏ_q`** — derived sorry-free.\n\nFor `q ≠ 0`, `q ≠ 1` the `q`-deformed kernel blows up at the\n`q`-Planck separation: `|[2]_q / (r² − ℏ_q²)| → ∞` as\n`r → ℏ_q` through `r ≠ ℏ_q`.  Genuine analysis (numerator is a\nnonzero constant, denominator tends to `0` and is eventually\nnonzero on the punctured neighbourhood since its only roots are\n`±ℏ_q` and `ℏ_q ≠ 0`), not a projected field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.qInt2_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.qInt2_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L86-L94","doc":"Over `ℝ` the `q`-integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` never vanishes for\n`q ≠ 0`: `q·(q + q⁻¹) = q² + 1 > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.hbarQ_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.hbarQ_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L78-L84","doc":"For `q ≠ 1` the `q`-Planck constant `ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹` is nonzero.\n(At `q = 0` one has `q⁻¹ = 0` and `ℏ_q = 1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.qDeformedKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.qDeformedKernel","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L72-L76","doc":"The `q`-deformed Möbius kernel of\n[`lem:nsi-q-deformed-kernel`]: `[2]_q / (r² − ℏ_q²)` as a\nfunction of the inter-point separation `r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.qInt2_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.qInt2_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L66-L70","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical bracket.** The longhand `q + q⁻¹` is this site's\nbody and its proofs use it, so the consolidation is the identity, not an alias.\nConditional: the two agree away from `q − q⁻¹ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.qInt2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.qInt2","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L62-L63","doc":"The `q`-integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/nsi_q_deformed_kernel.lean#L59-L60","doc":"Substrate `q`-Planck constant `ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}